From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:48:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] dt-bindings: soc: qcom: pmic-glink: Describe a charge
 current cooling device

The battery management firmware behind pmic-glink accepts a limit on the
battery charge current, which is what vendor thermal policies lower when
a device runs hot while charging.

Let a board list its charge current steps, highest first. With them the
pmic-glink node is a cooling device with one state per step, which the
thermal zones' cooling maps can refer to.

The idea and the property name follow Doctor Logix's Perpetua kernel
(denialwm/linux-perpetua 6fc72fc36e8c); the text is our own.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml        | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml
index 5c46a74c0a60..a336c47ff3a0 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,pmic-glink.yaml
@@ -66,6 +66,18 @@ properties:
   '#size-cells':
     const: 0
 
+  '#cooling-cells':
+    const: 2
+
+  qcom,charge-current-limits-microamp:
+    description:
+      Battery charge current steps for thermal mitigation, highest first.
+      With this property the node is a cooling device with one state per
+      step; state 0 leaves the charge current to the firmware, state N caps
+      it at the Nth step.
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 32
+
   orientation-gpios:
     description: Array of input gpios for the Type-C connector orientation indication.
       The GPIO indication is used to detect the orientation of the Type-C connector.
@@ -95,6 +107,9 @@ patternProperties:
 required:
   - compatible
 
+dependencies:
+  '#cooling-cells': [ 'qcom,charge-current-limits-microamp' ]
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
